{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Position Loop Tuning\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The position loop PID parameters are automatically calculated based on the selected bandwidth and payload when the {\b Apply} button is clicked.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It's also possible to manually enter the position loop PID parameters of an axis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Input the value for each parameter to store it, so it can later be applied. The value of each parameter must be an {\b integer}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Once all position loop parameters are set up, press {\b Apply} to apply them. Otherwise, press {\b Cancel} to restore the parameters to their original values.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Only {\b DC Brush} and {\b Brushless DC Motors} are supported. The textboxes will be greyed out for unsupported motors.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The following position loop PID parameters can be changed:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Kp}: PID Proportional Gain\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Ki}: PID Integrator Gain\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Ilimit}: PID Integrator Limit\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Kd}: PID Derivative Gain\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b DerivativeTime}: PID Derivative Time\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Kout}: PID Output Gain\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Kvff}: Velocity Feedforward Gain\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Kaff}: Acceleration Feedforward Gain\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Once applied, these settings may be stored in the motion controller's NVRAM so they persist across power cycles by clicking on the {\b Write to NVRAM} button.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note, the axis will be de-energized before the changes are written to NVRAM.\par}
}